e it wasn't odd it was a lot I  think to the outside world yes I think  it can be odd I mean I'm not oblivious  to what it sounds like but when you're  actually there in that atmosphere and  you're around it and you're watching  movies those kids - yes with this  it's very innocent but I think the fault  of my uncle was he just he didn't have  that bone in his body to look at it the  other way his naivety was his downfall  that's what hurts me more than anything  is knowing his innocence but then  knowing how the world is in early 1994  Jackson settled a civil suit with a  family of jordan chandler a boy who had  accused the pop star of sexually abusing  him despite paying over 22 million  dollars in that settlement jackson  continued to surround himself with young  children there are interviews with  michael where he has said sure people  spent time in my bed it was loving it  was a fun time it was pure and anyone  who thinks anything other than that just  has a dirty mind that had said from the  outside world looking in it is very odd  you all don't think that it's odd that  he would spend time let me say something  when we grew up coming up traveling on  the road we was older but Marlon and  Michael was much younger they never had  a regular childhood life Michael always  had been a kid at heart always he loved  Disney Land he loved those so he tried  to create that world himself he loved  that world he loved making kids happy  his whole life was to to make the whole  world come together yes he said that's  what it's all about especially children  he loved that I mean I think just  knowing my uncle and spending thousands  and thousands of hours with them he  would always ask us questions like what  was this like what was it like going to  a birthday party you know because he  didn't have that he thought vicariously  through me and my brothers and you know  his nephews none of you at any time said  you know Michael this doesn't look good  I know your intentions are pure but this  doesn't look good none of you at any  time said that to him I didn't you did I  did I did I asked him I said maybe you  should just hang around family and he  said well that I'm not doing God's work  then I'm not helping people I'm not my  uncle always like to help people  that was my uncle's purpose that's what  he felt he was doing and he felt he  connected with kids because that was his  childhood as you sit here today are you  worried about what this documentary will  do to his legacy no no  but it does seem to be a day of  reckoning for many of you and we don't  want to get in the way of that but you  have to shine the light brightly on both  sides yeah I think you know you'll have  to watch the documentary and decide for  yourself I think The Jacksons clearly  support their brother and when people  say it's all about money they said they  don't get any money from the Jackson  estate they wanted to make that very  clear the people that get the money or  Michael Jackson's three children and you  know Wade and James when we here you  know he didn't have a childhood he was  very childlike I think when you hear the  documentary you may rethink what does  that really mean  raises a lot of very interesting  questions
 

